comments.message:
This is wrong since 

formatSerialNumber('12345678')
// returns "12:34:56:78"

formatSerialNumber('1234567890')
// returns "12:34:56:78:90"

is clearly formatted. 

Either let's do something like: 
```
// only format when there is at least one A-F hex character
if (/^[0-9A-Fa-f]+$/.test(serial) && /[A-Fa-f]/.test(serial)) {
  return serial.match(/.{1,2}/g)?.join(':').toUpperCase() ?? serial.toUpperCase();
}
```

'AABBCCDD'   -> 'AA:BB:CC:DD'
'12345678'   -> '12345678'
'1234ABCD'   -> '12:34:AB:CD'
'hello'      -> 'hello'

Or maybe reword this to not be so bold.
